      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Character LoRA captioning (JoyCaption Beta One)\n\nReads every `.jpg/.jpeg/.png/.webp` in **image_dir** (no subfolders) and writes `<same name>.txt` **next to each image**.\n\n- **image_dir**: absolute path, e.g. `/home/mauro/datasets/venera`.\n- **custom_prompt** (JoyCaption Advanced): your captioning instruction. Edit the word limit (`60 words`) and what to include/exclude. Keep calling her `the woman`. If you clear it, `prompt_style` + `caption_length` + the optional Extra Options node are used instead.\n- Model: `joycaption-beta-one` (bf16 weights, auto-downloaded to `models/LLM/` on first run) loaded as `Maximum Savings (4-bit)` (~8GB VRAM). Uncensored, built for LoRA dataset captions.\n  - **Do not use `Balanced (8-bit)`**: bitsandbytes int8 segfaults (kills the whole server) when ComfyUI core's `comfy_kitchen` is loaded.\n  - **Do not use `joycaption-beta-one-fp8`**: its FP8 checkpoint loads with broken weights under transformers 5.\n- **Trigger tag prefix**: prepends `s3xyv3n3r4, ` to every caption in code (more reliable than asking the model). Change `string_a` per character.\n- **overwrite** on the saver: true replaces existing `.txt` files. When false, it writes `name_01.txt` instead of skipping.\n- `temperature` 0.6 is the default; lower it (0.3) for more consistent captions across the dataset.\n- Launcher: `mauro-files/run.sh` (no special VRAM flags needed)."
      ]
    },
